window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Weston will not break me, no matter how hard he tries.</b></p> <p>Lennox Holt never expected to venture outside of her castle walls, least of all to seek out the mythical island of Dawnlin to cure her mother. Searching for the healing waters was only one of the many challenges the island forced upon the Voyagers, and learning to trust Dawnlin and those already on the island wasn’t as effortless as she expected.</p> <p>Now, while in the clutches of the enemy, Lennox struggles with feeling unworthy as she desperately tries to escape, and return to her new home. She was warned of the manipulations and motivations of the Castaways, but as the future queen, she was trained for situations like these.</p> <p>She must find her inner strength and fight her deep-seated fears of inadequacy, without falling for the barrage of games and manipulations. The looming presence of the Castaway’s leader makes it difficult to follow through with her plans, so she must play games of her own to get the aggravating and infuriatingly enticing leader to trust her enough to let his guard down.</p> <p>But after living fully immersed on the other side, discovering more about those around her, and being told a story very different from the one she knows, she begins to question everything. Lennox now has to decide who she can trust, and most of all, who is telling the truth.</p> <p><i>Blade of Truth </i>is the second book in The Dawnlin Trilogy, for New Adult Fantasy Romance listeners who love a slow burn, enemies to lovers, forced proximity, forbidden romance, found family, and the one bed trope. It is meant for adult audiences with some spicy scenes.</p>"; 
